HOW THE CODE WORKS
AUTHENTICATION

The app uses:

DefaultAzureCredential

with these exclusions:

ExcludeEnvironmentCredential = true
ExcludeManagedIdentityCredential = true

That means it avoids environment-based credentials and managed identity for this exercise, and instead uses the available interactive/Azure CLI-based auth path the lab expects.

SECRET CLIENT

The app creates:

var client = new SecretClient(new Uri(keyVaultUrl), new DefaultAzureCredential(options));

This is the main SDK object used to talk to Azure Key Vault.

CREATE SECRET

The CreateSecretAsync method:

prompts for secret name
prompts for secret value
creates a KeyVaultSecret
stores it with SetSecretAsync
LIST SECRETS

The ListSecretsAsync method:

gets all secret metadata using GetPropertiesOfSecretsAsync()
loops through each secret
fetches full values using GetSecretAsync(secretProperty.Name)
prints name, value, and creation time

That exact pattern is what the lab text uses.
